---
description: Prefer SQL WHERE filters over loading rows then filtering in JS
alwaysApply: true
---

# SQL filtering

When rows already live in Turso, **filter in SQL** (or via repo params that become SQL). Do not `getAll*()` then `.filter()` in application code.

Use shared scope helpers when the filter is league/gender: `ListScopeParams` / `buildListScopeFilter` (`packages/database/src/utils/list-scope.ts`), and pass `{ leagueIds, genders }` into repos (`getTeams`, `getCategories`, `getAllMatches`, `getLeagues`, etc.).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — fetch everything, discard in JS
const teams = (await db.getTeams()).filter(
  (team) => allowedLeagueIds === null || allowedLeagueIds.has(team.league_id),
);

// ✅ GOOD — scope in the query
const teams = await db.getTeams({
  leagueIds: allowedLeagueIds ? [...allowedLeagueIds] : null,
  genders: allowedGenders ? [...allowedGenders] : null,
});
```

## When JS filter is OK

- Data is not in the DB yet (e.g. federation HTML before upsert)
- The predicate cannot be expressed cleanly in SQL (rare; prefer extending the repo)

Prefer adding optional params on the repository over a one-off in-memory filter.
